WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:03.120
- [Narrator] This little
old lady is Button,

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.360
a 21-year-old margay.

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.283
Her name comes from the
phrase “cute as a button.”

00:00:09.697 --> 00:00:12.290
(bright music)

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:14.710
The margay is a tree-dwelling cat

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:18.770
native to the dense forests
in Central and South America.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:21.310
These expert climbers will hunt, sleep,

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:23.880
and even give birth in the trees.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.540
The margay's wide feet and flexible toes

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.600
allow them to climb, jump,
and hang from tree limbs.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.220
Their long heavy tails
keep the animal balanced,

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:36.260
and their large eyes make them
excellent night hunters,

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:40.610
preying on birds, reptiles
and even small primates.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:43.740
Margays will hardly ever
cross open treeless areas,

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.900
making them extremely
sensitive to deforestation.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.530
In addition, the illegal
fur and pet trades

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.780
have made this wildcat a
near-threatened species.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:55.380
The best hope for the
margay's continued survival

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.250
is to preserve their
natural forest habitat.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:00:59.703
This is the margay.

